        "reasoning": "Excellent match. Author explicitly classifies as MVT. Limestone host rock is diagnostic for MVT. Sphalerite-galena-pyrite assemblage with trace element compositions (tetrahedrite-tennantite, jordanite-geocronite solid solutions) are characteristic of MVT deposits. Low-temperature hydrothermal fluids, vein and replacement textures in carbonate host, Pb-Zn-Ag-Cu-Sb-Ge metal associations all align perfectly with MVT classification. Dolomite gangue is typical."
